+Native bounded OneNote text reader
+
+scoped_onenote.py is a Python port/adaptation of parts of onenote_parser from:
+https://github.com/msiemens/onenote.rs
+Commit de3a64e8159c684b137ded89c3fef3c17272ec1d
+Upstream license: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (copy: scoped_onenote.LICENSE).
+Upstream author/copyright: retain the original repository notices; source files
+carry no separate per-file author/copyright statements at this commit.
+
+Ported design and format interpretation:
+- onestore/desktop/file_structure/{header,transaction_log_fragment,file_node_list,
+  file_node_list_fragment,parse_context}.rs
+- onestore/desktop/file_node/{mod,file_node_chunk_reference,global_id_table,
+  object_declaration,object_revision,object_space_manifest,revision_manifest,
+  root_object_reference,shared}.rs
+- onestore/desktop/objects/{root_file_node_list,object_space,revision_manifest_list,
+  revision,object_group_list,global_id_table,id_mapping,object}.rs
+- onestore/shared/{compact_id,object_prop_set,object_stream_header,prop_set,property}.rs
+- one/property/{mod,object_reference,object_space_reference,references,simple}.rs
+- one/property_set/{section_node,page_series_node,page_manifest_node,page_node,
+  title_node,outline_node,outline_element_node,outline_group,rich_text_node,
+  table_node,table_row_node,table_cell_node}.rs and onenote/page.rs.
+Paths are relative to crates/parser/src/.
+
+This derivative file remains MPL-2.0. On distribution of an executable/package
+containing it, make this covered source (including modifications) available under
+MPL-2.0 and inform recipients how to obtain it; retain this notice and license.
+MPL file-level duties do not relicense unrelated files in a larger work.
+No upstream fixtures are embedded in product code.
+
+Accepted profile and limits:
+- Desktop .one section signature; OneStore format 109ADD3F-911B-49F5-A5D0-1791EDC8AED8;
+  all four version fields = 42; current default-context revision role 1.
+- Committed transaction prefix only, cumulative .one CRC including earlier
+  sentinels; strictly increasing list counts (a newly created list may have 0,
+  as in real upstream fixtures). After the committed limit, transaction/list
+  tail references and physical append data are ignored as MS-ONESTORE requires.
+- Bounded fragment, node, revision, global-ID and property decoding; section ->
+  page series -> page object-space -> manifest -> page -> title/body order.
+- Unicode text takes precedence over extended ASCII (Latin-1). NUL-terminated
+  Unicode is supported; nonzero content after a NUL refuses. Invalid UTF-16
+  never falls back to an alternative property. Hidden runs are suppressed.
+- Titles come from the first current title outline, excluding date/time outlines;
+  cached current-page title is used only if no title object is present.
+- Images, ink and embedded files are reported as explicit non-text markers. Their
+  payload is never emitted, executed, extracted or fetched. No attachment path
+  is followed. Rich-text embedded-object references are unsupported and refuse;
+  stored plain math text is not evaluated. Unsupported active content refuses.
+- 16 MiB pure decoder input, 100000 nodes/objects/references, 4096 lists,
+  8192 revisions, 64 levels, 4096 properties per set, 4 MiB individual property,
+  2 MiB decoded text, 2000000 aggregate decoder work units. Existing read_file
+  routes further limit input to 1000000 bytes. Checkpoints honor call cancellation.
+- No .onepkg, .onetoc2, FSSHTTPB/sync-store decoding, encrypted sections, editing,
+  rendering, OCR, ink recognition, Office application validation or whole-format
+  acceptance. Successful reads are explicitly PARTIAL current-text coverage.
+
+Integrity scope:
+Transaction CRC, sizes, fragment sequences, revision ancestry/roles, global-ID
+resolution, property/reference counts, immutable read-only object declarations,
+and selected semantic edges are checked. Auxiliary read-only MD5, free-space
+lists, hashed-chunk deduplication and reference-count override CRC are not used
+to establish the textual view. They are not an authentication guarantee. The
+upstream parser also ignores these auxiliary checks. Read-only MD5 values in the
+two supplied producer fixtures do not equal a direct hash of their referred
+padded property blobs; this reader does not silently relabel that as a valid MD5.
